92186045417 true] [17592186420365 1080 "0.056" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420365 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420365 1083 #uuid "ddd4b49b-3871-5ead-9a7d-e5c9ef7a0761" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420366 1080 "0.156" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420366 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420366 1083 #uuid "ee4df031-007e-5fce-a926-ac3f42667005" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420367 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420357 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420367 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420358 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420367 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420362 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420367 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420365 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420367 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420366 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420367 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420367 1077 "selection" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420367 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420357 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420367 1079 #uuid "304334c9-f645-591e-bc70-9dbb97961017" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420368 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420355 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420368 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420368 1077 "field-1" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420368 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420355 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420368 1079 #uuid "723b37c8-0318-5da2-874d-1c31332f782d" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420369 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420356 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420369 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420359 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420369 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420360 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420369 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420361 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420369 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420364 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420369 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420369 1077 "selection" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420369 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420359 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420369 1079 #uuid "a3d02abe-a662-5d74-8d74-1566af6e8ecc" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420370 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420363 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420370 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420370 1077 "field-1" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420370 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420363 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420370 1079 #uuid "d29ba2bc-6b0d-55f1-9a0b-b4874a45e108" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420371 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420367 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420371 1069 "q-84756" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420371 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420371 1071 "A student who answers randomly has a $50%$ chance of correctly answering each question on a $12$-question test. What is the probability that the student selects exactly $10$ correct answers? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420371 1072 #uuid "01dbc8f6-a3cd-5172-a886-7310e77fa973" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420371 1074 "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of correct answers that the student gets.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=12$ questions\n\n- the probability of hitting each question is $p=50%=0.5$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(12,0.5).$ We want to find the probability of getting $x=10$ correct answers.\n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSubstituting the above information into the formula for probability mass function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=10) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{12}{10})(0.5)^{10}(1-0.5)^{12-10} \\\\  & =\\frac{12!}{10!(12-10)!}(0.5)^{10}(0.5)^{2} \\\\  & =66(0.5)^{10}(0.5)^{2} \\\\  & =0.016\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420372 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420370 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420372 1069 "q-276040" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420372 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420372 1071 "An unfair coin has an $80%$ chance of landing on heads. The coin is tossed $5$ times. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, what is the probability that the coin landed on heads at least four times?\n\nRounded to $3$ decimal places, the probability is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420372 1072 #uuid "2532926b-6b81-5b1e-a7b4-0b4cbbf77029" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420372 1074 "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times the coin landed on heads.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- There are $n=5$ tosses.\n\n- The probability of landing on heads is $p=80%=0.8.$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(5,0.8).$ \n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSubstituting the above information into the formula for the probability mass function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{x})(0.8)^{x}(1-0.8)^{5-x} \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{x})(0.8)^{x}(0.2)^{5-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that the coin landed on heads at least $4$ of the $5$ games. So, we compute\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 4) & =P(X=4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{4})(0.8)^{4}(1-0.8)^{5-4}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{5})(0.8)^{5}(1-0.8)^{5-5} \\\\  & =5(0.8)^{4}(0.2)+1(0.8)^{5} \\\\  & ≈0.737,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420373 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420369 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420373 1069 "q-130421" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420373 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420373 1071 "Ann has a collection of $20$ pairs of shoes, $12$ of which are sports shoes. Every working day she randomly picks a pair of shoes to go to work, and she has to work for $26$ days next month. What is the probability that she will choose a pair of sports shoes exactly $10$ times? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420373 1072 #uuid "790209a3-d18d-523b-a83b-f000e1032859" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420373 1074 "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of times Ann will choose a pair of sports shoes in those $26$ days.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=26$ working days next month\n\n- since there are $12$ pairs of sports shoes out of $20$ pairs in the collection, the probability that she will pick a pair of sports shoes on a given day is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{12}{20}=\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(26,\\frac{3}{5}).$ We want to find the probability of $x=10$ successes.\n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSubstituting the above information into the formula for probability mass function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=10) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{26}{10}){(\\frac{3}{5})}^{10}{(1-\\frac{3}{5})}^{26-10} \\\\  & =\\frac{26!}{10!(26-10)!}{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{10}{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{26!}{10!16!}{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{10}{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{16} \\\\  & ≈0.014\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420374 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420368 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420374 1069 "q-331639" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420374 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420374 1071 "A wildlife camera detects animals with a $40%$ success rate. The camera is triggered $7$ times during the night. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, what is the probability that it detects an animal at least $3$ times?\n\nRounded to $3$ decimal places, the probability is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420374 1072 #uuid "8e763d61-0831-5bdd-b6c6-c5e10a44b471" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420374 1074 "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times the camera successfully detected an animal.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- There are $n=7$ triggers.\n\n- The probability of detection is $p=40%=0.4.$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(7,0.4).$\n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSubstituting the above information into the formula for the probability mass function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{x})(0.4)^{x}(1-0.4)^{7-x} \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{x})(0.4)^{x}(0.6)^{7-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability of detecting an animal at least $3$ times. This corresponds to $P(X\\ge 3).$\n\nHowever, computing\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 3)=P(X=3)+P(X=4)+…+P(X=7)\n$$\n\nwill involve many computations, so let's express our answer in terms of the complement instead. By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 3) & =1-P(X<3) \\\\  & =1-[P(X=0)+P(X=1)+P(X=2)] \\\\  & =1-[(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{0})(0.4)^{0}(0.6)^{7-0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{1})(0.4)^{1}(0.6)^{7-1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{2})(0.4)^{2}(0.6)^{7-2}] \\\\  & =1-[(0.6)^{7}+7(0.4)(0.6)^{6}+21(0.4)^{2}(0.6)^{5}] \\\\  & =1-0.419\\,904 \\\\  & ≈0.580,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420375 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420376 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420375 1062 #uuid "2105619e-8693-5c1a-b9c4-86f38be603c4" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420375 1063 #edb/ref 17592186420373 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420376 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420377 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420376 1062 #uuid "29cfbfba-2513-567f-b12d-fc0e4b4fa288" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420376 1063 #edb/ref 17592186265970 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420377 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420378 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420377 1062 #uuid "5b5b31f0-1b55-5e0a-8163-ed1fa2d9dca0" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420377 1063 #edb/ref 17592186420372 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420378 1062 #uuid "63b8acd1-de5d-58b3-b19d-30965be2a286" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420378 1063 #edb/ref 17592186420374 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420379 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420375 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420379 1062 #uuid "7e04be3f-fd63-5a74-ad92-baa1c03bd6c7" 13194139534372 17592186045417 true] [17592186420379 1063 #edb/ref 17592186420371 13194139534372 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-8e2ae5f5-fad4-5930-b4b2-be1adc26af67" 17592186420354 "answer-2d415ee2-ce66-5299-b7c3-7e5330a401ce" 17592186420355 "answer-31d54eb6-7a30-5f6b-bd3e-dc209bc41ee0" 17592186420356 "answer-52b8ddff-6335-5